Revision history for Red::Driver::DuckDB

{{$NEXT}}
    - Derive named source tables and views through Red's table formatter (PersonCopy becomes person_copy).
    - Reject duplicate source names without altering existing tables, views or their generated-ID sequences.
    - Support quoted source names and reject names containing NUL.

0.0.5  2026-11-15T15:37:58Z
    - Fix source model .^all iteration to yield individual rows without an explicit slip.
    - Accept an optional :name on all source readers to name the generated Red model and derive its temporary SQL table/view name using Red's normal name conversion.
    - Document :name in source reader examples and add regression coverage for naming and iteration.

0.0.4  2026-11-15T07:34:09Z
    - Precompile the driver before timed launcher tests to avoid cold-compilation timeouts on Windows CI.
    - Add CSV, JSON, Parquet, text, blob and XLSX readers that return dynamically generated Red models.
    - Query sources through temporary read-only views by default; support writable snapshots with :materialize and generated primary keys.
    - Retain the source connection across queries, hydration, projections, joins and CRUD outside the original dynamic scope.
    - Infer column types, normalize attribute names and expose original names through .^source-columns.
    - Inflate nested lists and structures as Raku arrays and hashes; reject unsupported types and compound writes explicitly.
    - Add configure-s3 with temporary secrets, AWS credential-chain and explicit-key authentication, and compatible endpoints.
    - Safely encode reader options and clean up temporary objects when source initialization fails.
    - Install File::Temp before testing DB::DuckDB on Linux to satisfy its undeclared test dependency.
    - Add reader, lifecycle and S3 configuration regressions, plus real MinIO, verified HTTPS and XLSX integration tests.
    - Run remote integration fixtures entirely through Raku and native tools, including the Linux CI job.

0.0.3  2026-11-15T05:20:29Z
    - Fix installation

0.0.2  2026-11-14T18:15:01Z
    - Prioritize DuckDB identifier validation over CommonSQL and quote dotted names in PRAGMA tests.
    - Work around DB::DuckDB archive extraction failure on Windows CI with a Raku installer.
    - Replace the macOS installer, test launcher and tool tests with Raku; remove the Python CI dependency.
    - Support quoted table and sequence names; reject empty or NUL-containing identifiers.
    - Execute SET and PRAGMA on the active session and retain PRAGMA query results.
    - Track transaction commands through SQL comments, including nested block comments.
    - Reject NUL-containing SQL while preserving embedded NUL and Unicode in bound text.
    - Preserve large integer parameters and timezone offsets when inflating timestamps.
    - Preserve collations during migration reconstruction and distinguish generated columns from default text.
    - Compare JSON numbers without decimal rounding or loss of integer precision.
    - Reject execution on closed connections and invalidate old statements and results after reopening.
    - Add regression coverage for connection lifecycle, SQL parsing, migrations and value precision.

0.0.1
    - Implement DuckDB ORM backend using DB::DuckDB 1.0.1.
    - Add sequence IDs, CRUD, relationships, transactions and schema introspection.
    - Preserve decimal, temporal, binary, UUID and JSON values.
    - Add integration tests and a macOS Alien installation workaround.
    - Verify sorted grouping and nested classify keys with real data.
    - Add native JSON operations, ordered schema removal, BOOLEAN constants and typed query-plan parameters.
    - Preserve reverse/tail NULL ordering and embedded-database test isolation.
    - Add SQL regex predicates, Unicode classes, scoped backreferences and exact whole-match text extraction.
    - Add a reproducible Red-suite launcher with separate TAP and diagnostic streams.
    - Add transactional migration execution, sequence planning and database-scoped migration locking.
    - Preserve atomic NULL filling and NOT NULL tightening with transactional reconstruction.
    - Declare unsupported savepoints and row locks explicitly, with capability-aware Red tests.
    - Package the matching Red companion patch and pin CI to reproducible Red sources.
